图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"LLM-free lossless* compaction engine for DeepSeek Harness","id":"gh:1333638979","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-compaction-instant","slug":"TsFreddie/dsh-compaction-instant","topics":["agent","compaction","context-compression","cordis","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"LLM-free lossless* compaction engine for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-compaction-instant"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Instant, near-lossless context compaction for DeepSeek Harness — a **drop-in replacement for `@deeps"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"eek-ai/dsh-compaction-basic`** that replaces LLM summarization with the deterministic conversation-c"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ompiler principle of lllyasviel/VCC."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"A compaction compresses a shadowed history span in **milliseconds, with zero model calls**, keeping "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"**original tokens only** — no paraphrase, no hallucination, no summarizer cost. Everything that is c"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ut is still recoverable through `(seq N)` pointers into the durable session log."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Key features"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **LLM-free** — compaction never invokes a model. No summarizer prompt, no inference latency, no to"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ken spend; the compile is deterministic text processing, so a million-token history compresses in mi"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"lliseconds.\n- **Near-lossless** — output contains only original tokens; every cut is marked and poin"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ts at its durable `seq`, and prior checkpoints are copied verbatim.\n- **Instant** — a single determi"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"nistic pass over the shadowed nodes; no network, no model, no KV-cache concerns.\n- **Contract-exact "},{"id":"p7s6","text":"drop-in** — same seam, events, provenance and failure vocabulary as `compaction-basic`; every built-"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"in preset loads it unchanged (alias install)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Example"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"A region containing a user request, an assistant text + tool call, and its result compiles to:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Every tool call is ONE line: the key argument for whitelisted tools (`toolArgTools`), name-only for "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"the rest (`* job_kill (seq 9 -> result 10)`), nothing at all for `hideTools` rows. Tool results neve"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"r occupy entries — the `-> result N` pointer keeps them one `recall(type:\"result\")` away. Long user/"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"assistant text is truncated to its budget with `...(truncated from seq N)`; every elision names the "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"durable event that still holds the full content."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Recall: the lossless read-back layer"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The package also ships the counterparts that close the near-lossless loop — **same-session recall** "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"for the agent and the human. Because the session log is append-only, every token the compiler ever e"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"lided is still recoverable:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Entry point | Module | What it does |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| `recall` **tool** (model-facing) | `dsh-compaction-instant/tool` | Typed restore: `type:\"seq\"` wit"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"h `(seq N)`/`(seqs A-B)` markers, `type:\"result\"` with the `result N` pointer, `type:\"checkpoint\"` w"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ith a `[checkpoint N]` ordinal — restores exact original content into the current tool result |\n| `s"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"earch` **tool** (model-facing, grep) | `dsh-compaction-instant/tool` | Keyword/regex search over the"},{"id":"p15s5","text":" whole durable log — including content elided by compaction — returning matching events with their `"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"(seq N)` pointers, ready for `recall` |\n| `/recall` **command** (human, grep) | `dsh-compaction-inst"},{"id":"p15s7","text":"ant/command` | `/recall <keyword|regex>` appends a durable `form: \"recall\"` user message with the ma"},{"id":"p15s8","text":"tching events and their seq pointers, so the next model turn sees them |\n| Shared cores | `dsh-compa"},{"id":"p15s9","text":"ction-instant/recall` + `dsh-compaction-instant/search` | Seq parsing (`12`, `3-7`, `seq 12` / `seqs"},{"id":"p15s10","text":" 3-7`), log expansion, budgets, projection; regex compilation and hit rendering |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Recall keeps **everything**: text, reasoning, raw tool-call arguments, nested tool-result content; l"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"og-only events render as labeled data dumps; missing seqs are reported; a `maxRecallTokens` budget ("},{"id":"p16s3","text":"default **16000**) cuts with a provenance marker and counts the skipped remainder; searches cap show"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"n hits (`maxSearchHits`, default **50**). Both plugins are separate rows, so they can be mounted nex"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"t to **any** compaction backend — they only read the durable log."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Every checkpoint also frames a short **RECALL guide** at its head, telling the model exactly how to "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"use `recall` / `search` to recover elided content. When a prior checkpoint is elided under cap press"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ure it never vanishes silently: it leaves a single `[checkpoint N]` line (N = compaction ordinal, 1 "},{"id":"p17s4","text":"= oldest), which `recall(type:\"checkpoint\", id:\"N\")` restores in full."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"All fields optional; defaults shown."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Key | Default | Meaning |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| `thresholdRatio` | `0.5` | Fraction of the routed model's context window that triggers automatic c"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ompaction |\n| `retainTurns` | `1` | Preferred complete recent turns kept verbatim (automatic and man"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ual `/compact`); never overrides the ceiling |\n| `retainTokens` | `5120` | **Hard** retained-region "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"token ceiling: older whole turns are added only while the total fits, and when the latest turn alone"},{"id":"p21s5","text":" exceeds it, only the fitting suffix of that turn is kept |\n| `auto` | `true` | Register `agent/pre-"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"step` pressure and `agent/request-error` overflow recovery |\n| `checkpointCap` | `65536` | Total bud"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"get for one compiled checkpoint (compiler tokens): a checkpoint compiled from a smaller span stays n"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"ear-lossless, a larger one elides down to this cap |\n| `maxTokens` / `checkpointScale` | `8192` / `0"},{"id":"p21s9","text":".1` | **Deprecated** — accepted for drop-in compatibility but **ignored**: the budget is the cap alo"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"ne (no floor, no proportional scaling) |\n| `textTokens` | `512` | Budget per assistant text block |\n"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"| `userTextTokens` | `1024` | Budget per user text block |\n| `toolCallTokens` | `128` | Budget per t"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"ool-call one-liner (never rescaled — see the elision rules) |\n| `toolResultExcerptTokens` | `256` | "},{"id":"p21s13","text":"Accepted for compatibility; **inert** — tool results no longer occupy entries |\n| `includeReasoning`"},{"id":"p21s14","text":" | `false` | Keep reasoning blocks in the checkpoint |\n| `stripNoiseXml` | `true` | Strip configured"},{"id":"p21s15","text":" noise wrappers from user text |\n| `noisePatterns` | see compiler | Noise XML regex sources, applied"},{"id":"p21s16","text":" with the `s` flag |\n| `toolKeyFields` | built-ins | Extra tool-name → argument-field map for one-li"},{"id":"p21s17","text":"ners |\n| `toolArgTools` | see compiler | Whitelist whose key argument renders in the one-liner (`rea"},{"id":"p21s18","text":"d`/`write`/`edit`/`glob`/`grep`/`bash`/`shell`/`web_search`/`skill`/`subagent`/…); every other tool "},{"id":"p21s19","text":"is name-only |\n| `hideTools` | — | Bookkeeping tools dropped from the checkpoint entirely |\n| `model"},{"id":"p21s20","text":"Policies` | — | Per provider/model overrides of `thresholdRatio`/`retainTurns`/`retainTokens` |\n[该节后"},{"id":"p21s21","text":"cies` | — | Per provider/model overrides of `thresholdRatio`/`retainTurns`/`retainTokens` |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Browser settings card (Settings → Plugins)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Tokenizer and multilingual behavior"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Guarantees"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
